  "articleBody": "Navigating an insurance claim for interior restoration after storm damage can be tricky, and it's easy to make a few common missteps that can complicate things. Here are some key mistakes to steer clear of:\n\n**Don't Sign Contracts Immediately.** It's tempting to jump on the first offer, but avoid authorizing full replacement work before your insurance company has had a chance to inspect and agree on the scope of damage. Focus on temporary mitigation first.\n\n**Don't Skip the Documentation.** Failing to thoroughly document all damage with photos and videos *before* any cleanup or permanent repairs is a big one. This visual evidence is crucial for your claim.\n\n**Don't Ignore Your Policy's Timeline.** Many policies have deadlines for reporting damage. Don't delay; contact your insurance company as soon as it's safe to do so, usually within 24-48 hours.\n\n**Don't Toss Receipts.** Keep meticulous records of any expenses related to the damage, even for temporary repairs. These can often be reimbursed.\n\n**Don't Assume Your Contractor Knows Insurance.** Make sure your chosen contractor has experience working with insurance companies and can provide estimates in a claims-friendly format, like line-item pricing. We're well-versed in working with adjusters to make the process smoother for you.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
